sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Cam as Camera (RTSP)
    participant Edge as Edge Pipeline
    participant Ingest as Backend Ingest API
    participant Outbox as Outbox Table (tx)
    participant Bus as RabbitMQ
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Notif as Notification Service
    participant Dash as Dashboard (WS/STOMP)

    Cam->>Edge: RTSP frame stream
    Edge->>Edge: MotionDetected (OpenCV MOG2 gate)
    Edge->>Edge: VehicleDetected (YOLOv11)
    Edge->>Edge: Plate box detection
    Edge->>Edge: OCR (PaddleOCR primary,\nEasyOCR/VietOCR comparators) -> PlateRecognized
    Edge->>Edge: ByteTrack assigns/updates track_id
    Edge->>Edge: Point-in-polygon: vehicle center -> ParkingSlot
    Edge->>Ingest: POST /api/v1/sites/{siteId}/ingest/events\n{eventId, occurredAt, type=VehicleEntered,\nplate, track_id, slot_id, snapshot}
    Ingest->>Ingest: validate idempotency (event_id)\n+ tenant/site scope from device auth
    Ingest->>DB: INSERT ParkingEvent (VehicleEntered) +\nINSERT Outbox row (same tx)
    DB-->>Ingest: committed
    Outbox->>Bus: relay publish VehicleEntered (outbox poller/CDC)
    Bus-->>DB: consumer updates Vehicle.current_slot_id,\nParkingSlot.status=occupied
    Bus-->>Notif: consumer sends NotificationSent (push/email/ws)
    Bus-->>Dash: consumer pushes live update
    Notif-->>Dash: NotificationSent delivered over STOMP/Redis relay
    Ingest-->>Edge: 202 Accepted {eventId}

    Note over Cam,Dash: TARGET flow. Today (§1) is simpler:\nsingle YOLOv5 plate+char model -> POST /api/vehicles/check-vehicle\n(JSON or multipart snapshot) -> VehicleLog row, no slot/tracking concept,\nno RabbitMQ/outbox, broadcast directly via STOMP /topic/vehicle-check
